__pycache__/
*.pyc
build/
*.egg-info/
*_repo_rewards_report.md
*_audit_report.md
*_readiness.md
*_low_findings.md
flexfactor_audit_batch_report.md

# Run artifacts: audit logs and probe output are per-run evidence, not source.
logs/
*_audit_run*.log
incognito_audit.log
probe_tiers_out.json

# Pre-proxy snapshots kept as the launcher's documented local revert path. The
# same content is already in git history (the commit before the fcc-proxy
# switch), so committing a second 380k copy would be pure duplication.
*.bak-preproxy

# Scout run artifacts. A scout run writes these into the CURRENT directory, so
# running scout from the FlexFactor checkout leaves them in the repo root as
# untracked noise (found there 2026-08-16). They are per-run evidence, not
# source - same class as the audit logs above.
_scout_report.json
.flexfactor-scout-proposals.json

# Generated by flexfactor_discovery: which CLI/Cursor/ai-time backends this
# PARTICULAR machine can reach. Committing it would hand another machine routes
# whose binaries it does not have, and every route would fail at call time and
# cool its pool. Regenerate locally with:
#   python -c "import flexfactor_discovery as d; d.write_auto_catalog()"
catalog.auto.json

# Run evidence written into the audited repo by FlexFactor itself (never committed)
*_run_manifest_*.json

# Secrets. FlexFactor takes every credential from the ENVIRONMENT (see
# .env.example for the full surface), so a .env in this checkout holds real
# provider keys. Its own readiness gate `gitignore_protects` is CRITICAL-
# adjacent for exactly this reason and was failing here until 2026-08-23.
# `.env.example` is the documented template and stays tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Per-run evidence written by a run started FROM this checkout (`runs/`), the
# same class as logs/ above: it is output, not source.
/runs/

# The interpreter README tells every owner to create (`py -3.12 -m venv .venv`).
# It was never ignored, so the documented install left thousands of
# untracked files in `git status` - and FlexFactor's own dirty-tree gate
# reads that status.
.venv/
venv/

# Managed mobile control-plane local dependencies and Vercel project metadata.
node_modules/
.vercel/

# Test debris: a literal "~" directory appears when a path with a tilde is
# used without expanduser. It is never legitimate repo content.
/~/
